script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'hardstop-c-panel',
  description: 'Hard stop (c) adversarial panel: security-auditor (all items) + reviewer concurrency/webhook + reviewer money/dates/UI on 4e34633..HEAD',
  phases: [{ title: 'Panel' }],
}
const CTX = `Timed build, working dir ./app. Source of truth ../BRIEF.md; contracts and decisions ../SPEC.md, ../DECISIONS.md (D1-D56). The brief overrides CLAUDE.md where SPEC.md says so (error body {error: string}; OPTIONAL Idempotency-Key header; NO webhook_events / replay window — webhook idempotency = bill FOR UPDATE + UNIQUE payments.gateway_bill_id; bigint sen; invoice status computed; seed via npm run seed; payments status updated in place under a guard trigger; storage has INSERT-only policy, reads via server 60 s signed URL). Everything is built now: all routes in the brief incl. POST /api/leases/:leaseId/gateway-bills and POST /api/webhooks/gateway (key test_x_signature_key; simulator gateway-sim.mjs), GET /api/gateway-bills/:billId, UI pages /login, /dashboard, /leases, /leases/[id], /tenant, /payments/return. Diff since the last panel: git diff 4e34633..HEAD (whole history: git log). Local stack up and seeded (password RentDemo#2026, publishable key in .env.local); dev server http://127.0.0.1:3000. Read-only: never edit files, never reset the DB; writes only against your OWN data: create bills/payments only on the seeded probe@northwind.test lease (C-01-7) or on rows you create inside rolled-back transactions; DB/HTTP probes via bash ../scripts/with-db.sh when they touch the DB. One simple command per Bash call.`
const FIND = { type: 'object', properties: {
  verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['PASS', 'FAIL'] },
  findings: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: {
    severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['blocker', 'major', 'minor'] }, area: { type: 'string' }, file: { type: 'string' }, line: { type: 'string' },
    repro: { type: 'string' }, fix: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['severity', 'area', 'repro', 'fix'] } } },
  required: ['verdict', 'findings'] }
const sec = agent(`${CTX}\nSecurity auditor for hard stop (c): run EVERY item of your checklist against the running stack as anon and every seeded role: PostgREST tables + rpc, Storage payment-slips (upload/read/list/sign with each role's token), every route handler incl. the webhook (forged, missing, replayed, duplicate-key, oversized, non-form bodies, unknown bill), the /payments/return page (it must never change state), server actions (there should be none), static secret checks (SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY or GATEWAY_X_SIGNATURE_KEY reachable from client code / NEXT_PUBLIC vars / the built .next/static bundle; getSession on server; user_metadata roles), logging of payloads. Reproducible findings only. Verdict PASS/FAIL (= SECURITY: PASS/FAIL).`,
  { agentType: 'security-auditor', label: 'panel-c:security-auditor', phase: 'Panel', schema: FIND })
const conc = agent(`${CTX}\nReviewer lens: CONCURRENCY + WEBHOOK + IDEMPOTENCY. Try to refute: one bill -> at most one payment under concurrent deliveries; a paid bill never goes back; failed -> paid works; signature algorithm (sort by char code, extra fields, timingSafeEqual, lowercase hex), the 401 -> 404 -> 422 -> state order, received_at = paid_at, unapplied_sen when invoices already paid, bill amount = unpaid due on or before MYT today, bill ids unguessable, lock order (bill -> lease vs lease -> payment) deadlock-free, cap races, approve twice, overlap race, optional Idempotency-Key replay semantics, retry-once on 40001/40P01, slip cleanup on failure. Read src/server/services/{webhook,gateway,payments}.ts, supabase/migrations/*.sql, tests/concurrency, tests/webhook. Report only real problems with a concrete scenario (reproduce with real requests on the probe lease where possible). PASS or FAIL.`,
  { agentType: 'reviewer', label: 'panel-c:reviewer-concurrency', phase: 'Panel', schema: FIND })
const ui = agent(`${CTX}\nReviewer lens: MONEY + DATES + UI. Try to refute: every date/time shown or accepted is Malaysia time whatever the server/browser TZ (formatMytDisplay, mytLocalToIso, datetime-local default, month labels), no hydration mismatches (Date/now/locale rendering that differs between server and client; toLocaleString without timeZone; new Date() in server render reused in client), amounts typed in ringgit parsed with parseRinggitToSen, receivedAt always sent with +08:00, toasts for success and error on every action, loading states, empty states, manager-only actions, void with confirmation + reason, slip upload validation (JPEG/PNG/PDF, 5 MiB) and the path <orgId>/<leaseId>/<uuid>.<ext>, tenant portal reads via supabase-js and computes statuses with invoiceStatus, amount due now, Pay now flow, phone edit, /payments/return read-only, no 'any', no secret key in client code. Read src/app/(app)/**, src/components/**, src/app/login/**. Fetch pages with curl as different roles if useful (build the session cookie as REFERENCE.md describes). Report only real problems with a concrete scenario. PASS or FAIL.`,
  { agentType: 'reviewer', label: 'panel-c:reviewer-money-ui', phase: 'Panel', schema: FIND })
const [s, c, u] = await Promise.all([sec, conc, ui])
const fails = [s, c, u].filter(r => r && r.verdict === 'FAIL').length
log(`panel c: security=${s && s.verdict} concurrency=${c && c.verdict} money-ui=${u && u.verdict}; ${fails}/3 FAIL`)
return { security: s, concurrency: c, moneyUi: u, failCount: fails }
